<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Kitts and Nevis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Federation of Saint Kitts and Nevis, Saint Christopher and Nevis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a> and Nevis, officially the Federation of Saint Kitts and Nevis, is an island country in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leeward-islands">Leeward Islands</a> of the Lesser Antilles in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. Saint Kitts hosted the first British and French Caribbean colonies, which divided the island between them after 1625, and its slave-based <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> industry made it the richest British colony per capita in the Caribbean by the 1700s. The islands were federated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anguilla">Anguilla</a> in 1882, joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> Federation from 1958 to 1962, and became an associated state with full internal autonomy in 1967. Anguilla seceded that year, and the federation of the two remaining islands gained full independence on 19 September 1983.</p></div>
